# Documentation guardrails (Design System)

## Content integrity

- **Never invent** system-specific facts, component behavior, token semantics, dimensions, or color values. Every stated value must come from Figma, token JSON, or an explicit design decision.
- If information is missing or unverified, write `TBD` and add an item under **Gaps / TBD**.
- No code examples for now (design-only documentation).

## Structure and consistency

- Use stable headings and the same section order for pages of the same type. See `component-doc-structure.mdc` for component pages.
- Every component doc should start with a one-line description immediately after the H1.
- Prefer tables for properties, states, and token mappings. Use consistent column order across all tables of the same kind.
- Apply page taxonomy from `docs-taxonomy.mdc` (`component`, `overview`, `foundation`, `workflow`) and keep scope boundaries clear.

## Token references

- Token names must match the JSON keys exactly and be wrapped in inline code (e.g., `` `Semantic.Color.Focus-Outline.Inner` ``).
- Always pair a token path with its resolved hex fallback — either in parentheses or in a dedicated table column.
- See `token-references.mdc` for naming conventions and formatting rules.

## Figma references

- Reference Figma by **component set name** and **property name** only.
- Never include Figma internal variable IDs (`VariableID:*`) in prose, tables, or YAML specs.
- Figma node IDs are allowed for traceability (for example, `node-id` in source URLs or explicit node references in metadata).
- Do not use node IDs as token identifiers; keep token references human-readable.

## Metadata

- Component docs must declare `doc_status` in frontmatter: `draft`, `ready`, or `needs-review` (see `markdown-lifecycle-status.mdc`).
- Component spec YAMLs must declare `status`: `draft` or `ready`.
- Generated files in `docs/_generated/` must not be hand-edited; they are overwritten by skills.

## Editorial consistency

- Follow language and tone rules from `docs-language-tone.mdc`.
- For component docs, include Figma traceability metadata from `component-figma-traceability.mdc`.
- Keep overview/index pages synchronized per `overview-index-maintenance.mdc`.
